    <p class="section-number">01 · Beverage-Air refrigerator not cooling</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three root causes our techs diagnose first across LA commercial.</h2>

    <p>A Beverage-Air commercial refrigerator that won't hold below 41°F usually traces to one of three root causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across LA County restaurants, bars, convenience stores, and hospitality kitchens. (1) Condenser fan motor failure year 5 to 9 — the most common single Beverage-Air service item across all series (HR, HF, SP, DP, UCR, MR, MMR). Head pressure climbs, cooling capacity drops, box temperature drifts up. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock. (2) Dirty condenser coil — restaurant kitchen grease and lint accumulate on the condenser fins. About 25 to 30 percent of Beverage-Air service calls resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with condenser cleaning, no parts charge. (3) Anti-condensation heater wire failure on MR / MMR glass-door merchandisers year 5 to 8 — the limiting factor on Beverage-Air merchandiser lifespan. $340 to $580 typical all-in.</p>

    <p>Beverage-Air is part of Ali Group, the Italian privately-held foodservice holding company (sister brands include Scotsman ice machines, Ice-O-Matic, Champion dishwashers, Carpigiani gelato). Manufactured in Winston-Salem, North Carolina since 1944. Mid-premium tier — between True / Traulsen at the top and Turbo Air at entry-tier. You see Beverage-Air everywhere in LA: chain restaurants standardize on it (Chipotle, Panera, Subway corporate accounts spec Beverage-Air across store buildouts), mid-tier restaurants and cafés use HR-Series reach-ins and SP-Series sandwich prep tables as default, convenience stores and gas stations use MR/MMR glass-door merchandisers for beverage retail, bars use UCR and LV undercounter for back-bar storage. See the broader <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/brands/beverage-air/">Beverage-Air brand pillar</a> for full lineup context.</p>

    <p><strong>$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair.</strong> BHGS Registration #A49573 and EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), plus R-290 propane certification for newer Beverage-Air green-refrigerant models (2020+). CSLB C-20 HVAC. BBB Accredited Business. 90-day warranty. Same-day across LA, OC, Ventura. Next-day Riverside and San Bernardino. Sister sub-services: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-cooler-not-cooling/">walk-in cooler not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/true-refrigerator-not-cooling/">True refrigerator not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/commercial-freezer-not-freezing/">commercial freezer not freezing</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/not-cooling/">generic commercial refrigeration not cooling</a>. Parent: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/">commercial refrigeration</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 DIAGNOSTIC SEQUENCE -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Five-step diagnostic on every Beverage-Air not-cooling call</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Cheap-first sequence across HR, SP, UCR, MR, MMR.</h2>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Box temperature documentation.</strong> Probe at product level (not air space at ceiling) to verify current product temperature against the operator's last log entry. Establishes HACCP CCP exceedance window for California Retail Food Code 41°F compliance.</li>
      <li><strong>Identify series and refrigerant.</strong> HR, HF, SP, DP, UCR, UCF, MR, MMR, MMF, LV, MTP, or SPED. Rating label refrigerant (R-134a legacy or R-290 propane post-2020) determines sealed-system service certification requirement.</li>
      <li><strong>Visual condenser inspection.</strong> Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulation on fins. If condenser is the diagnosis, cleaning runs $200 to $280 and resolves the call without parts on 25 to 30 percent of LA Beverage-Air service visits.</li>
      <li><strong>Condenser fan motor amp draw and rotation.</strong> Multimeter at fan motor terminals against rated spec, visual rotation check. Most common single Beverage-Air service item across all series. $320 to $520 replacement.</li>
      <li><strong>MR/MMR anti-condensation heater test (merchandisers only).</strong> Continuity test on glass-door anti-condensation heater wire. Open circuit confirms failure. $340 to $580 replacement. Limiting factor on MR/MMR merchandiser lifespan year 5 to 8.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Most diagnostics complete in 25 to 40 minutes on-site. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair walk operators through the findings with photo documentation before any repair work begins. Sealed-system work on R-290 propane Beverage-Air models requires both EPA 608 Universal certification (#1346255700410) and R-290 hydrocarbon certification, which we hold and document on every Beverage-Air post-2020 service visit.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TOP CAUSES FREQUENCY -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · Top causes by frequency</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Across LA County Beverage-Air service calls.</h2>

    <p>Across LA County Beverage-Air commercial refrigerator service calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run — Chipotle, Panera, Subway chain locations with HR-Series reach-ins, mid-tier restaurants and cafés with SP and DP prep tables, convenience stores and gas stations across Long Beach and Inland Empire with MR/MMR merchandisers, bars across West Hollywood and Hollywood with UCR and LV back-bar storage, hotels with the full lineup — the failure breakdown clusters predictably.</p>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Condenser fan motor failure (25-30% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Most common single Beverage-Air service item across all series. Year 5 to 9 typical wear curve. Head pressure climbs without fan circulation, cooling capacity drops, box temperature drifts up. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock for common shaded-pole motor sizes. Common across HR, HF, SP, DP, UCR, MR, MMR series.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Dirty condenser coil (20-25% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulate on condenser fins. Resolves at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning on 25 to 30 percent of Beverage-Air service calls, no parts charge. Standalone deep cleaning $200 to $280.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Anti-condensation heater wire — MR/MMR merchandisers (15-20% of merchandiser calls)</h3>
      <p>Anti-condensation heater wire in glass door frame open-circuited. Year 5 to 8 typical wear. Glass fogs progressively, eventually drips. $340 to $580 replacement requires partial frame disassembly. Limiting factor on MR23, MR45, MMR45+ merchandiser lifespan.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Cold rail evaporator fouling — SP/DP prep tables (12-15% of prep table calls)</h3>
      <p>Lettuce drippings, tomato juice, sauce splash accumulate on the evaporator coil above the cold rail. Heat transfer drops, cold rail drifts warm. Deep evaporator cleaning resolves 90 percent of cold rail running warm calls without parts replacement. $200 to $340 typical deep clean. SP, DP, MTP, SPED prep configurations all share this pattern.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>5. Door gasket year 5-7 (10-15% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Compression set, tearing, magnetic seal failure. Warm air infiltration, defrost cycle overwhelmed, frost buildup or temperature drift. $180 to $340 replacement covering HR-Series, HF-Series, SP-Series, DP-Series, UCR27, UCR48 dimensions stocked on truck.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>6. Defrost timer + compressor + evaporator fan (8-12% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Defrost timer on HF freezer variants $280 to $440. Evaporator fan motor year 5 to 9 $320 to $520. Compressor failure year 10 to 13 inland or 8 to 11 coastal $1,400 to $2,200 all-in. Combined these resolve the remaining 8 to 12 percent of Beverage-Air not-cooling calls.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

